<title>SWEDEN: MoDo 9-mo profit tumbles 43 pct.</title>
<headline>MoDo 9-mo profit tumbles 43 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry company MoDo resutls for the nine months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 2,469  vs  4,319</p>
<p> Sales				     14,999  vs 17,261</p>
<p> Operating costs			 11,334  vs 11,905</p>
<p> Non-recurring items			 11  vs    282</p>
<p> Associate interests			  5  vs     46</p>
<p> Depreciation				 916  vs    847</p>
<p> Operating profit			 2,765  vs  4,837</p>
<p> Net financial items	     CHARGE 296  vs    518 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					    796  vs  1,111</p>
<p> Net profit				 1,673  vs  3,208</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full company name is MoDo.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of 14 analysts gave an average forecast for a profit after financial items of 2.24 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
